# Private terms the commit hooks refuse in the staged tree and in commit messages.
# scripts/install-git-hooks.sh copies this file to .git/sensitive-terms.txt the
# first time; edit THAT copy. It lives inside .git, so it is never committed or
# pushed, which is the point: a list of private names cannot itself be public.
#
# One term per line, matched as plain text ignoring case. Blank lines and lines
# starting with # are ignored. Add anything a scanner cannot know is private,
# for example (remove the leading # to activate):
#
# your-employer-name
# your-client-name
# internal-hostname.example
# /Users/your-username
# /home/your-username
